From 1f2550fccc975d4da3fbd240eaa9b2b91485b3b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crxssrazr93 <crxssrazr93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:49:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ruffle_sdl: software mouse cursor overlay and SDL colour
 cursor

ruffle_sdl hides the OS cursor, so a gamepad driven mouse (gptokeyb right stick
mouse, a uinput mouse) is invisible. Add two optional remedies.

Software cursor (RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR=1 or --sw-cursor): a small arrow drawn as one
GLES 3.0 quad on the window framebuffer after the movie blit and before the
buffer swap, in window pixels (works with --render-size and letterboxing).
Shown after SDL MouseMotion, hidden after RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR_IDLE_MS (default 2000)
without motion, zero work while hidden. Every GL state item touched is saved and
restored, since wgpu owns the context. RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR_SIZE (default 24 px) sets
the height, RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR_IMAGE loads a PNG instead of the built in arrow.
The frame is redrawn when only the cursor changed.

SDL colour cursor (RUFFLE_SDL_CURSOR=1): SDL_CreateColorCursor from the same
bitmap and shows the SDL cursor. Only works where the video driver draws cursors
(X11, Wayland), not on fbdev or KMSDRM without a hardware cursor.
